From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:42:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 434/434] wifi: mt6797: survive a frame the air lost

Any management or EAPOL frame the access point did not acknowledge ended
the lifetime with -ENOLINK, and Wi-Fi then stayed down until a module
reload. On channel 6 this followed the access point's own
deauthentication.

Report the frame as unacknowledged and go on: mac80211 and the supplicant
retry what matters. A lost deauthentication counts as one that timed out,
so the cleanup still runs. Also stop refusing the wait on the last frame's
acknowledgment, which turned the same loss into the same failure.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
index 86f11fb0c..7b01c41b3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
@@ -2510,10 +2510,12 @@ void mt6797_mac_join_work(struct work_struct *work)
 					mt6797_mac_data_tx_counted(mac, ack);
 					continue;
 				}
-				if (!ack) {
-					ret = -ENOLINK;
-					goto failed;
-				}
+				/* A frame the air lost is mac80211's and the supplicant's
+				 * to retry, not a fault; a lost deauthentication still
+				 * ends the lifetime through the cleanup.
+				 */
+				if (!ack && completed_internal)
+					mac->ccmp_deauth_timeouts = 1;
 				continue;
 			}
 			/* Post-stop (window over), the exact TX-done above is the only owed
@@ -2905,8 +2907,6 @@ int mt6797_mac_join_wait_management(struct mt6797_mac *mac)
 		if (ktime_get_ns() >= deadline || mac->join_inflight)
 			return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
-	if (!mac->join_last_acked)
-		return -ENOLINK;
 	if (mac->join_page_debt) {
 		mac->join_credit_deadline = min_t(u64, mac->join_deadline,
 						  ktime_get_ns() + 100 * NSEC_PER_MSEC);
-- 
